# SPA fallback, scoped to the two routes that are NOT prerendered.
#
# Every other client route is emitted as a real HTML file by
# scripts/prerender.js (/, /about, /contact, /sitemap, /terms, /privacy) and is
# served as a static asset. A blanket `/* /index.html 200` is deliberately not
# used: it shadows those files on static servers that apply the fallback before
# checking for an asset, and it also answers every unknown URL with a 200 app
# shell — soft 404s, which Google treats as a quality signal. Unmatched paths
# now 404 properly.
#
# Adding a client route means either adding it to ROUTES in
# scripts/prerender.js, or adding a fallback line here.
#
# These point at app-shell.html, not index.html: index.html is the prerendered
# landing page, and serving it here would hand every bike detail page a canonical
# pointing at the homepage before JS runs. app-shell.html is the bare shell.
/bikes/*      /app-shell.html   200
/unsubscribe  /app-shell.html   200
